Z||000011||Spektrum-87GT||12-16-2001||05:26 PM||||to anyone that liked the monkey island games... here are some others that you would like by lucasarts:<P>Loom<BR>Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade(the adventure one... one of my all time faves!)<BR>Indiana Jones and the Fate of Atlantis<BR>Sam and Max Hit the Road<BR>Zak McKraken<BR>Full Throttle<BR>and of course... the original... Maniac Mansion(and its sequal of course... Day of the Tentacle)<P>All of the sierra quest games are good too, especially the police quests. Dynamix put out a really great adventure game called The Adventures of Willy Beamish... corny name but a great game.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/spektrum_87gt/" TARGET=_blank>87 Fiero GT</A><BR>1991 Jeep Cherokee<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://members.home.com/bspracklin1/sig2.jpg">   <BR>AIM:<FONT COLOR="red">S</FONT><FONT COLOR="purple">p</FONT><FONT COLOR="blue">e</FONT><FONT COLOR="cyan">k</FONT><FONT COLOR="green">t</FONT><FONT COLOR="yellow">r</FONT><FONT COLOR="orange">u</FONT><FONT COLOR="red">m</FONT><FONT COLOR="purple">1</FONT><FONT COLOR="blue">1</FONT><FONT COLOR="cyan">7</FONT><BR>And no! i'm not gay dangit!||||reg||1
Z||000012||loafer87gt||12-16-2001||06:23 PM||||Did any of you guys ever play the orginal text based Hero's Quest by Sierra? What a hell of a game. Those were some of the best days of my life playing the old Sierra games such as Hero's Q and the Police Quest games on my old Amiga. Just for nostalgia's sake, here is a site that has all the sountracks for the Sierra games.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.queststudios.com/quest/sierrap1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.queststudios.com/quest/sierrap1.html</A> ||||reg||1
